-- title:
--   Genus of X_H(M) is unchanged at primes ℓ ∤ M
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a natural number with $M \neq 0$ and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$; write $\Gamma_H(M) =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) for the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained by pushing forward along the inclusion of $\Gamma_0(M)$ the preimage under `gamma0Units M` of $H$. Let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $M$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $\ell$. Two function fields are compared. On the one hand [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldC k M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L76) is the intermediate field of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by the set `intFormRatiosC k (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)` of Laurent series attached to $\Gamma_H(M)$. On the other hand [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldBar M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L123) is the intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, for $\bar{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, generated over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the image under the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb` of the corresponding field over $\mathbb{Q}$, namely the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by `intFormRatiosC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)`. The conclusion is an equality of genera in the sense of `genusFF`, that is of the dimension over the base field of the first cohomology $H^1$ of the zero divisor (a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on the places of the extension): the genus of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldC k M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L76) over $k$ equals the genus of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldBar M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L123) over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is Igusa's good-reduction theorem for the modular curve $X_H(M)$ at primes not dividing the level, stated in the language of one-variable function fields: the characteristic-$\ell$ function field generated by the reductions of $q$-expansion ratios has the same genus as its characteristic-zero counterpart. It is combined with the reverse inequality [`ModularCurve.genusFF_xHFunctionFieldBar_le_genusFF_xHFunctionFieldC_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.genusFF_xHFunctionFieldBar_le_genusFF_xHFunctionFieldC_of_not_dvd), and is used downstream in the study of the Jacobian of $X_H(M)$ and of reductions of $q$-expansions modulo $\ell$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_genusFF_xHFunctionFieldC_eq_genusFF_xHFunctionFieldBar_of_not_dvd.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_XH
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
